structure.module_docstring:
The allosteric gate: exact arithmetic, no activation on silence, an honest quorum.

Counterexamples from the study (`domain/allostery.py`):

- float arithmetic with a non-integer Hill coefficient (2.5);
- `activation_threshold=0` activated with no signal at all (H(0) = 0 >= 0);
- large inputs raised a bare `OverflowError`;
- the "quorum" was a threshold on the sum, so one large sensor activated it;
- the signals were a list, so one caller could repeat itself and count twice.

Package documentation claims only what the code does (study defect D19).

Counterexamples removed on 2026-09-29, each checked here so it cannot return:

- the package docstring claimed "exponential half-life decay", "Regulatory
  T-Cell supervision" (which lives in OEWAS) and "phagocytic formulary
  regeneration";
- `immune_bench.py` said it phagocytoses refused turns from CemeterySink; it
  only escapes caller-supplied phrases;
- `mssn_ports.py` evaluated "the 7 frozen Demo 3 failure detectors" with three
  codes;
- `mssn_classifier.py` listed AM-FSP-6 as a classified failure mode, but no
  detector emits it;
- `mssn_pharmacy.py` called itself a "Faithful Python port" of `pharmacy.rs`.

classes.docstring:
The detector that produced the matches, and what it evaluates itself.

`predicates` are the host danger kinds the detector already evaluates;
`offsets_are_content` says whether match offsets locate text in the content.

functions.docstring:
BOUND bindings for the skill scripts listed in ``script_executors.yaml``.

A listed script must sit in its own skill package and have a ``__main__`` guard;
``test_script_executors.py`` checks that each one starts.

structure.module_docstring:
OEWAS reaches the Epistemic Immune System only through `ImmuneScreenPort`.

Counterexamples:

- the OEWAS domain imported the OEEIS domain (`domain/workflow_graph.py`,
  `domain/planar_substitution.py`, `domain/capability_catalog_v1.py`);
- (review, 2026-09-29) the port accepted `detector_id=None` and then ran the
  unchecked gate, so a Signal 2 derived from Signal 1 suppressed a substitution;
- (review) the port took `Sequence[object]` instead of records it owns;
- (review) `quorum_verdict([1, 1])` from one caller activated the quorum.

